The example meeting (ui/example/fr, ui/example/en) is an invented meeting of two voices, made by
scripts/example.py. No real meeting and no real person are in it.

Synthetic voices generated with ElevenLabs: the model Eleven Multilingual v2, asked through
OpenRouter's speech API on 2026-11-27, speed 0.95. French: the voices « lily » (« Vous ») and
« eric » (Hugo). English: « will » (« Vous ») and « matilda » (Jess).

The sound is Kitokey's to use, as these terms say (read on 2026-11-27):
  ElevenLabs, Terms of Service, https://elevenlabs.io/terms-of-use: section 4(c)(ii), « as between
  you and ElevenLabs, you retain all rights in and to your Output »; section 1(c), paid users
  « may use the Services for commercial purposes ».
  OpenRouter, Terms of Service, https://openrouter.ai/terms: section 6.1, « Your ownership rights in
  the Output are set forth in the Model Terms for each Model you use ».

Changes: the service's speech is resampled to 24,000 samples a second, laid out on two tracks and
kept as FLAC.
